  "response_text": "In this lab, we allocated a new stack for the Process Stack Pointer (PSP) by first obtaining the initial value of the Main Stack Pointer (MSP). We calculated a new PSP value by subtracting an offset of 0x400 from the initial MSP value to reserve a separate region of memory for the PSP. This ensured that the PSP had its own dedicated stack space, avoiding any overlap with the MSP. Knowing the initial MSP value was important because it helped us position the PSP in a contiguous location to the MSP, at a fixed distance that determined the amount of memory allocated to the MSP.\\n",
